Run `{{command}} instructions {{intent}} {{target}} -- '<guidance>'` and follow what it
prints: the instructions of this turn, written for it.

- `{{target}}` is {{target_help}} in the prompt; without one, the command
  uses the one of the current worktree.
- `<guidance>` is the rest of the prompt, in single quotes, with each `'`
  written as `'\''`. Leave out `-- '<guidance>'` when there is none.
{{flags}}
End every turn with the record they describe, through the `turn_end` tool of
the {{name}} MCP server, else `{{command}} turn end`. The user's answer comes as
your next prompt; a long one says to run `{{command}} turn answer {{target}}`. If a
command fails, report its error and stop; never run the turn without its instructions.
